# BMad Method tool scaffolding (agent personas, installer config) -- not
# part of the Naka submission, and several of its files embed the local
# installer's username in output explicitly marked "regenerated on every
# install" / "scoped to YOU personally". Kept out of what has to be a
# public repo entirely, same as .agent/.agents/.claude below.
.bmad-loop/
_bmad/
_bmad-output/

# Naka build artifacts
# build/ is deploy/build.sh's staging dir: the full vendored dependency
# tree (boto3, botocore, cedarpy's compiled .so, ~4100 files, ~80MB) it
# installs before zipping. Not naka/pkg/ -- that path doesn't exist; the
# real one is naka/build/pkg/, and the stale pattern let the whole tree
# through untracked-but-stageable until this was scanned for.
naka/build/
naka/dist/
naka/**/__pycache__/
naka/.venv/

# OS/editor junk, wherever it turns up
**/.DS_Store
**/Thumbs.db
**/desktop.ini

.agents/
.claude/
.agent/
prompt_optimizer/
